## Why This Is Asked
This question tests cross-platform native module design, real-time constraints, memory management, and safe bridging with JavaScript.

## Key Concepts
- Real-time audio pipeline, native threads, DSP paths, and cross-platform bridging
- Lock-free data structures, sample-rate negotiation, backpressure handling, and deterministic scheduling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal API usage sketch
import { startEngine, feedInput, onProcessed, stopEngine } from 'NativeAudio';

startEngine({ sampleRate: 48000, channels: 1 });
feedInput(inputBuffer, length);
onProcessed((processedBuffer) => { /* handle processed audio */ });
stopEngine();
```

## Architecture Considerations
- **Threading**: Run audio processing on a dedicated high-priority thread (real-time priority on Android, a dedicated dispatch queue on iOS) separate from the JS thread to avoid blocking.
- **Memory**: Use lock-free ring buffers and pre-allocated buffer pools to ensure zero allocations on the hot path.
- **Backpressure**: Implement a bounded queue with clear semantics for what happens when the input buffer fills—either drop frames, signal overflow, or block gracefully based on the use case.
- **Sample-rate changes**: Negotiate sample rate at engine start; if the device doesn't support the requested rate, fall back to the nearest supported rate and notify JS.
- **Fallback**: Detect DSP capability at runtime; if unavailable, either gracefully degrade or expose a clear error indicating the device lacks required hardware support.

## Why This Is Asked
Tests offline caching, data merging by id, and simple hook design for React Native with AsyncStorage.

## Key Concepts
- AsyncStorage usage for simple persistence
- useEffect/useState lifecycle and dependency on endpoint
- Merging lists by id while preserving user-visible order
- Exposing a small API (data, loading, error, refetch) for components

## Code Example
```javascript
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';

export function useCacheList(endpoint) {
  const [data, setData] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const loadData = async () => {
      try {
        // Load cached data first
        const cached = await AsyncStorage.getItem(`cache_${endpoint}`);
        if (cached) {
          setData(JSON.parse(cached));
        }

        // Fetch fresh data
        const response = await fetch(endpoint);
        const freshData = await response.json();

        // Merge by id, preserving cached order
        const merged = mergeById(data, freshData);
        setData(merged);

        // Update cache
        await AsyncStorage.setItem(`cache_${endpoint}`, JSON.stringify(merged));
      } catch (err) {
        setError(err);
      } finally {
        setLoading(false);
      }
    };

    loadData();
  }, [endpoint]);

  return { data, loading, error, refetch: () => loadData() };
}

function mergeById(cached, fresh) {
  const map = new Map();

  // Preserve cached order
  cached.forEach(item => map.set(item.id, item));

  // Update with fresh data
  fresh.forEach(item => {
    if (map.has(item.id)) {
      map.set(item.id, item);
    } else {
      // Append new items
      cached.push(item);
    }
  });

  return Array.from(map.values());
}
```

## Component Example
```javascript
function EventsList() {
  const { data, loading, error } = useCacheList('/api/events');

  if (loading) return <ActivityIndicator />;
  if (error) return <Text>Error: {error.message}</Text>;

  return (
    <FlatList
      data={data}
      keyExtractor={item => item.id}
      renderItem={({ item }) => <EventCard event={item} />}
    />
  );
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests designing a robust offline-first data store with CRDTs, native modules, and careful backpressure for React Native UIs, plus encryption and delta synchronization considerations.

## Key Concepts
- CRDTs: OR-Set for fields, RGA for ordered lists; per-record envelopes
- Delta-based synchronization and backpressure control
- JSI/TurboModule bridging; AES-GCM encryption at rest
- Conflict resolution: per-field last-writer-wins with server tie-breaker
- Failure modes: partial synchronization, divergence, encryption/key rotation

## Code Example
```javascript
// RN usage sketch
import {NativeCRDTStore} from 'react-native-crdt-store';

const store = new NativeCRDTStore({
  encryptionKey: 'base64-key',
  syncEndpoint: 'https://api.example.com/sync'
});

// Create inspection record
const report = await store.create('inspection', {
  technicianId: 'tech_123',
  timestamp: Date.now(),
  items: ['item1', 'item2'] // RGA for ordered items
});

// Offline updates automatically merge
await store.update(report.id, {
  status: 'completed',
  notes: 'Inspection finished'
});

// Sync with backpressure awareness
store.startSync({
  batchSize: 100,
  maxConcurrency: 3
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to architect a small, performant UI component in React Native with responsive layout and simple in-memory caching, mirroring real-world gallery features.

## Key Concepts

- FlatList with dynamic numColumns
- useWindowDimensions for responsive layout
- In-memory LRU cache for images
- onViewableItemsChanged for preloading
- Memory safety and eviction strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
import React, { useMemo, useRef } from 'react';
import { FlatList, Image, TouchableOpacity, useWindowDimensions } from 'react-native';

export function ImageGrid({ images, onTap }) {
  const { width } = useWindowDimensions();
  const columns = width < 600 ? 2 : 3;
  // simple cache placeholder
  const cache = useRef(new Map()).current;

  const renderItem = ({ item, index }) => (
    <TouchableOpacity onPress={() => onTap(index)}>
      <Image source={{ uri: item }} style={{ width: width / columns, height: width / columns }} resizeMode="cover"/>
    </TouchableOpacity>
  );

  return (
    <FlatList
      data={images}
      keyExtractor={(uri, i) => uri + '-' + i}
      renderItem={renderItem}
      numColumns={columns}
      removeClippedSubviews
    />
  );
}
```

